---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import {defaults,limits} from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-12/solver.mjs';
const base='/equipment/03-12/', manual='https://harrickplasma.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/PDC-32G-2-UserManual-2025-v3.pdf', product='https://harrickplasma.com/plasma-cleaners/basic-plasma-cleaner/';
const labels={gaugeW:'Invented frame width (mm)',gaugeD:'Invented frame depth (mm)',xMm:'Enclosure X offset (mm)',yMm:'Enclosure Y offset (mm)',yawDeg:'Virtual rotation (°)'};
---
<Layout pageTitle="Harrick PDC-32G-2 · static exterior footprint" description="Inspect the static enclosure of a PDC-32G-2 and compare its nominal box with an invented rectangle. No treatment or operation is simulated." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment hp"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-12/">← Equipment 03-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#hp-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">03-12 · DOCUMENTARY EXTERIOR / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Harrick PDC-32G-2</h2><p>Inspect a static exterior and see how rotating its nominal footprint affects clearance in an invented bench frame. No instrument operations or surface treatment are simulated.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Static tabletop enclosure</h3><div id="hp-view" aria-label="Orbitable Harrick enclosure with fixed front window, knob silhouettes and rear fan shell"></div><div class="bar"><button data-hp-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-hp-view="rear">Rear</button><button data-hp-view="top">Footprint top view</button><button id="hp-grid">Hide invented frame</button></div><p id="hp-ready" role="status">Loading metric exterior…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The two colored markers on top only change the virtual footprint. Real-looking controls, door, and connectors are fixed visual geometry.</p></section>
<section><h3>Independent geometry exercise</h3><canvas id="hp-diagram" width="700" height="340" aria-label="Top-view outlines of invented bench frame and rotated rectangular enclosure"/><div class="fields">{Object.entries(labels).map(([k,label])=><label>{label}<input id={'hp-'+k} type="number" min={limits[k][0]} max={limits[k][1]} step="any" value={defaults[k]}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="bar"><button id="hp-inspect" class="primary">Check footprint</button><button id="hp-quarterTurn">Toggle 0° / 90°</button><button id="hp-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="hp-status" aria-live="polite">Try the centered 0° case, then turn 90° to see the shallow frame become too small.</p><output id="hp-result">No footprint report yet.</output><button id="hp-export" disabled>Export footprint JSON</button></section></div>
<section id="hp-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected model: <a href={product}>Harrick Basic PDC-32G-2</a>, 2025 exterior. Harrick’s <a href={manual+'#page=12'}>manual Fig. 3, p. 12</a> supplies front and rear photographs for this exact variant; <a href={manual+'#page=41'}>p. 41</a> gives nominal overall dimensions. Details such as knob proportions and grille bars are inferred. Not a mechanical drawing, OEM fit certification, or installation guide. No internal or external accessories were reconstructed.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="640" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original render showing black front face, fixed viewing window and decorative controls"/><figcaption>Original front view, not a photograph. Compared with Fig. 3A for window, control positions and shell.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="640" height="440" src={base+'rear.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rear render showing fixed fan grille and connector silhouettes"/><figcaption>Original rear view, compared with Fig. 3B. Blanks are geometric stand-ins only, without functional connections.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Reference</th><th>What was verified</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Nominal outer dimensions</td><td>10 × 8 × 8.5 inches W × D × H, Harrick p. 41</td><td>254 × 203.2 × 215.9 mm nominal shell and feet; decorative protrusions and badges excluded from the teaching footprint.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Centered 280 × 230 mm invented frame</td><td>13.0 mm left/right, 13.4 mm front/back</td><td>Exact; 10⁻¹⁰ mm analytical tolerance. These margins are not clearances on real equipment.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rotate 90°</td><td>203.2 mm projected width, 254 mm depth</td><td>Exact nominal projection; −12 mm on each shallow side, static interference in the invented frame.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Proposed surface eligibility test</td><td>Treatment/eligibility expiry</td><td>Not implemented or run. This release contains no surface-treatment model.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The rotated width is <code>|W cos θ| + |D sin θ|</code>; depth is <code>|W sin θ| + |D cos θ|</code>. Center offsets subtract from one side and add to its opposite. Positive margins fit inside the teaching rectangle, zero denotes contact, and negative denotes geometric interference. No access, ventilation, installation, hoses, electrical state, safety reserve, cleaning or activation is modeled. JSON preserves the frame and enclosure dimensions, offsets, revision and derived margins.</p>
<p><a href={base+'pdc32g2-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-report.json'}>Output format example</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR inspection action contract</a>. No physical headset or equipment test claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-12/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.hp{max-width:76rem}.hp .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.hp section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.hp .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.hp .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.hp label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.hp input,.hp button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.hp button{cursor:pointer}.hp button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.hp .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.hp #hp-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.hp #hp-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.hp #hp-diagram,.hp img{width:100%;height:auto}.hp #hp-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.hp #hp-status.error{color:#a54a34}.hp .scroll{overflow:auto}.hp table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.hp td,.hp th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.hp figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.hp .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
